! ja_ax1a "IBOX-1", routine IBP30-IBP53, p.37 (octal 004614.00-
! 004652.40): "%V-ICR% ADD TO VALUE %-% IMMED., COUNT, + REFILL".
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  V-ICR was one of EIGHT modeled index operations a
! coverage screen found in ZERO of the 140 programs run_tests.sh
! references, all eight then confirmed by poisoning them at once (277
! sections still passed).  ibox1_vic_chain closed V-IC from the facing
! page; this is its companion and closes V-ICR.
!
! WHAT IS ACTUALLY NEW HERE, since most of the block's length is
! operations that already have coverage.  SR appears in ibox1_vpicr,
! ibox3_lr and ibox4_prog_ix_v; V+ICR's refill path is closed by
! ibox1_vpicr.  The new surface is V-ICR's own count-and-refill arm --
! exercised BOTH ways, refilling and not -- and the IBP30-IBP32 trick
! below, which has no parallel anywhere in the suite.
!
! THE REFILL TEST IS THE REASON TO WANT THIS BLOCK.  IBPA4 is not a
! constant, it is TWO INSTRUCTIONS: a NOP and a B,IBP33, sharing one
! word.  IBPA3 carries count 1 and refill IBPA4, so the single V-ICR at
! IBP30 drives the count to zero, the refill reloads the index register
! FROM THAT WORD, and SX then writes it straight over IBP31 -- where it
! is immediately executed as the two instructions it always was.  A
! refill that does not happen leaves IBP31 holding the decremented
! index word instead, control falls into IBP32's BD,$ and THE MACHINE
! STOPS.  An index word and an instruction pair are the same 64 bits,
! and the deck uses that identity as its test.
!
! THE OTHER TWO TESTS are a V-ICR that must NOT refill (count 2 -> 1)
! and one that must (count 1 -> 0, refilling from IBPA6), each feeding
! the same self-modifying branch chain ibox1_vic_chain uses: the value
! goes over one link, and the count and refill are summed -- SC/LV for
! the count, SR/LV for the refill, V+ COM04 for the branch opcode, then
! V+ IBPSTO to add them, which is what the listing calls "ADD C+R" --
! and stored over another.
!
! THE ARITHMETIC, derived before this was ever run.  IBPA5 seeds value
! = IBP51+.36, count 2, refill IBPA6:
!
!   IBP34  V-ICR 2.32, no refill  -> IBP46 = 4643.04 (IBP49)
!          C+R = 1*64 + IBPA6*64 + 4 -> IBP52 = 4652.04 (IBP53)
!   IBP40  V-ICR 0.32, REFILLS    -> IBP50 = 4646.04 (IBP52)
!          C+R = 4*64 + IBP46*64 + 4 -> IBP49 = 4644.04 (IBP50)
!
! so the chain runs IBP46 -> IBP49 -> IBP50 -> IBP52 -> IBP53, and all
! four manufactured links are on it.  Every address matches the
! listing's own comments.  (As in ibox1_vic_chain, those comments
! annotate two of the four "BE" where the encoding is BD -- COM04's +4
! sets IBM bit 21 and the branch code at bits 19-21 is BE = 000,
! BD = 001.  Both branch unconditionally, so the chain is unaffected.)
!
! IBP47, IBP48, IBP51 and IBPSTO are not links: IBPSTO is the scratch
! the C+R sum passes through, and the others are padding that keeps the
! link addresses where the arithmetic puts them.
!
! IBP53's two VFs are MEANT to be executed as NOPs, and the listing
! writes the same value twice in different bases -- "%8=777777.70" and
! "262143.56" -- which assemble identically.

        SLC, (8)6104.0
ISTOZ   DD(BU,64,8), 0
ISTOY   DD(BU,64,8), 0
COM04   VF, 0.04

        SLC, (8)4614.0
IBP30   LX, $X1, IBPA3                       ! set up XW
        V-ICR, $X1, 2.0                      ! should refill
        SX, $X1, IBP31
        NOP, 0.0
        CNOP
IBP31   BE, $                                ! becomes NOP, (8)525252.0
        BE, $                                ! becomes B, IBP33
IBP32   BD, $                                ! hang up
IBPA3   XW, IBPA3+0.34, 1, IBPA4             ! common XW
IBPA4   NOP, (8)525252.0
        B, IBP33                             ! refill XW
IBP33   LX, $X1, IBPA5                       ! set up XW
IBP34   V-ICR, $X1, 2.32                     ! shouldnt refill V-2.32
IBP35   SV, $X1, IBP46                       ! store value
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
IBP36   SV, $X1, IBPSTO
        SR, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        V+, $X1, COM04
IBP37   SV, $X1, ISTOZ
        LV, $X1, ISTOZ
IBP38   V+, $X1, IBPSTO                      ! add C+R
IBP39   SV, $X1, IBP52                       ! store C+R
        LV, $X1, IBP46
        NOP, 0.0
IBP40   V-ICR, $X1, 0.32                     ! should refill
IBP41   SV, $X1, IBP50                       ! store value
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
IBP42   SV, $X1, IBPSTO
        SR, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        V+, $X1, COM04
IBP43   SV, $X1, ISTOZ
        LX, $X1, ISTOZ
IBP44   V+, $X1, IBPSTO                      ! add C+R
IBP45   SV, $X1, IBP49                       ! store C+R
        LX, $X1, ISTOZ
        CNOP
IBP46   BE, 0
        BD, $                                ! becomes BD, IBP49 + BD, $
IBP47   BE, 0
        BD, $
IBP48   BE, 0
        BD, $
IBP49   BE, 0
        BD, $                                ! becomes BE, IBP50 + BD, $
IBP50   BE, 0
        BD, $                                ! becomes BE, IBP52 + BD, $
IBP51   BE, 0
        BD, $
IBP52   BE, 0
        BD, $                                ! becomes BD, IBP53 + BD, $
IBPSTO  BE, 0                                ! store area
        BD, $
IBPA5   XW, IBP51+0.36, 2, IBPA6             ! common XW
IBPA6   XW, IBP52+0.04, 4, IBP46             ! refill XW
IBP53   VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, 262143.56                        ! executed as NOP,-.32
PASS    BEW, $
        END, IBP30
